      "math_academy_id": "q-71398",
      "knowledge_point_id": "74f126da-5f3b-5af8-9aee-d6f0a4c61c49",
      "knowledge_point": "Determining the Shape of a Level Curve",
      "problem": "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+2y}$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $c=0$ gives a circle\n\nII. $c=1$ gives a hyperbola\n\nIII. $c=2$ gives a parabola",
      "worked_solution": "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+2y} & =c \\\\ {x}^{2}+2y & ={c}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=0$ then the level curve is $y=-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2},$ which is not a circle.\n\n- If $c=1$ then the level curve is $y=\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2},$ which is not a hyperbola.\n\n- If $c=2$ then the level curve is $y=2-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2},$ which is a parabola.\n\nSo, only statement III is true.",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
